ion interface{…}An object specifying the format that the model must output.Configuring `{ \"type\": \"json_schema\" }` enables Structured Outputs, which ensures the model wi", "title": "Responses | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/go/resources/responses"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn13search4", "snippet": "ResponseFileSearchCallSearchingEvent { item_id, output_index, sequence_number, type } ... Configuring `{ \"type\": \"json_schema\" }` enables Structured Outputs, which ensures the model will match your su", "title": "Responses | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/typescript/resources/responses"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn13search5", "snippet": "In addition to supporting JSON Schema in the REST API, the OpenAI libraries for Python and JavaScript also let you define object schemas using `pydantic.BaseModel`", "title": "Structured model outputs | OpenAI API", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs?api-mode=responses&trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn13search6", "snippet": "An object specifying the format that the model must output.Configuring `{ \"type\": \"json_schema\" }` enables Structured Outputs, which ensures the model will match your supplied", "title": "Get a model response | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/responses/methods/retrieve"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn13search7", "snippet": "beta_response_file_search_call_in_progress_event: object { item_id, output_index, sequence_number, 2 more } ... Configuring `{ \"type\": \"json_schema\" }` enables Structured Outputs, which ensures the mo", "title": "Responses | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/beta/subresources/responses"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn13search8", "snippet": "You can use Structured Outputs with the new SDK helper to parse the model’s output into your desired format, or you can specify the JSON", "title": "Structured model outputs | OpenAI API", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn13search9", "snippet": "* `code_interpreter_call.outputs`: Includes the outputs of python code execution in code interpreter tool call items. ... This can be useful for storing additional information about", "title": "Create a model response | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/python/resources/responses/methods/create"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn13search10", "snippet": "An object specifying the format that the model must output.Configuring `{ \"type\": \"json_schema\" }` enables Structured Outputs, which ensures the model will match your supplied", "title": "Responses | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/java/resources/responses"}, {"type": "text_result", "domain": "developers.openai.com", "ref_id": "turn13search11", "snippet": "Setting to `{ \"type\": \"json_schema\", \"json_schema\": {...} }` enables Structured Outputs which ensures the model will match your supplied JSON schema. ... A description of", "title": "Create chat completion | OpenAI API Reference", "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/chat/subresources/completions/methods/create"}]}}
